    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1292">

                <pb facs="1173" n="915" xml:id="pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123E16/92a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Minister in Roumania, Servia, and Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Vopicka</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-18T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>166. Department’s 165, 16th,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1292-f1"/> intended that
                    Einstein, now presumably awaiting instructions Bucharest should proceed to Sofia
                    if the Bulgarian Government has expressed its willingness to receive him in
                    capacity of Chargé d’Affaires and that on his arrival in Sofia he will assume
                    charge of British interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
